# cahunRules: hunting hours, hunter orange, conveyances, roads and prohibited methods.
# Sources: FWCA ss. 1, 17, 18, 20, 23 to 30; O. Reg. 665/98 ss. 26, 33, 55 to 57, 63 to 66,
# 80, 86, 91, 92; Hunting Regulations Summary 2026 (general regulations, turkey, black bear,
# important messages).
SEG = "RUL"
CAT = "cahunRules"
Q = [
('In Ontario, outside the exceptions, how long before sunrise may hunting begin?',
 'Half an hour', ['One hour', 'Fifteen minutes', 'Not until sunrise'],
 'Section 20 of the Act bans hunting from half an hour after sunset to half an hour before sunrise, so legal hours run from half an hour before sunrise to half an hour after sunset.'),
('After legal hours, a hunter is walking out of the bush with a rifle. How must it be carried?',
 'Unloaded and encased', ['Unloaded with the action open', 'Unloaded with the safety on', 'Loaded with the safety on'],
 'From half an hour after sunset to half an hour before sunrise, a firearm in an area usually inhabited by wildlife must be unloaded and encased.'),
('For the night firearm rule, when is a firearm considered encased?',
 'Enclosed on all six sides', ['In a sleeve open at the muzzle', 'Held in a closed truck rack', 'Wrapped fully in a blanket'],
 'The Hunting Regulations Summary says that to be encased, a firearm must be enclosed on all six sides, as in a closed gun case.'),
('Which is the main exception that allows hunting at night in Ontario?',
 'Raccoon hunting with a licensed dog', ['Coyote hunting with a light', 'Bullfrog hunting with a gun', 'Deer hunting with a light'],
 'Section 80 lets a small game licence holder hunt raccoon at night, with a light, only when accompanied by a dog licensed for hunting.'),
('During spring wild turkey season, what is the latest time a hunter may hunt each day?',
 '7:00 p.m.', ['Sunset', 'Noon', 'Half an hour after sunset'],
 'The summary says spring turkey hunting runs from half an hour before sunrise to 7:00 p.m., an exception to the normal hours.'),
('When must a licensed hunter wear hunter orange?',
 'Deer, elk, moose gun seasons and bear season', ['Only in gun seasons for deer and moose', 'Only while hunting big game with a gun', 'Only on Crown land in gun seasons'],
 'Section 26 requires a hunter orange garment and head cover while hunting during the open seasons for deer, elk or moose (other than bows-only seasons) and during the open season for bear, with exemptions such as a bear hunter in a tree stand.'),
('During a gun season for deer, a bow hunter is hunting rabbits. Must they wear hunter orange?',
 'Yes, orange is required', ['No, bow hunters are exempt', 'No, small game hunters are exempt', 'Only the head cover is needed'],
 'The rule applies to all licensed hunters during a gun season for deer, elk or moose, including bow hunters, falconers, small game hunters and trappers hunting on their licence.'),
('What minimum area of hunter orange must the garment show above the waist?',
 '400 square inches', ['200 square inches', '100 square inches', '1,000 square inches'],
 'The garment must be solid hunter orange of at least 400 square inches (2,580 square centimetres) above the waist, visible from all sides, plus a hunter orange head cover.'),
("Which hunter orange vest fails Ontario's rule?",
 'A front and back panel only', ['A solid vest with silver stripes', 'A solid vest under a small pack', 'A solid jacket with a logo'],
 'The orange must be visible from all sides, so a vest of only a front and rear panel may not qualify. Reflective stripes are fine if 400 square inches of orange remain.'),
('Which statement about the hunter orange head cover is correct?',
 'It may have open mesh', ['It may be camouflage orange', 'It may be any bright colour', 'It is optional with a vest'],
 'The garment must be solid and not open mesh, but the head cover may have open mesh and a brim of another colour. Neither may use camouflage orange.'),
('Which hunter is exempt from hunter orange during a gun season for deer?',
 'A duck hunter', ['A woodcock hunter', 'A grouse hunter', 'A coyote hunter'],
 'Hunters of double-crested cormorants and migratory game birds are exempt, except woodcock hunters, who must wear it.'),
('A licensed bear hunter, in a bear season with no gun season for deer, elk or moose, sits in a tree stand. Is orange required?',
 'No, not while in the tree stand', ['Yes, at all times while hunting', 'Only the hunter orange head cover', 'Only when hunting on Crown land'],
 'During the bear season, a bear hunter who is in a tree stand is exempt from the bear season orange rule. Orange is still required in a gun season for deer, elk or moose.'),
('A deer hunter uses a ground blind during the rifle season. What does the summary say?',
 'Wear orange in the blind too', ['Orange can come off inside', 'Orange on the blind replaces it', 'Only the head cover is needed'],
 'Hunters in ground blinds must wear hunter orange even inside the blind, and are advised to make the blind visible, for example with orange material on the outside.'),
('Under the Act, when may a loaded firearm be in a boat while hunting?',
 'When paddled with no motor', ['When the motor is shut off', 'When the boat is anchored', 'When drifting with no power'],
 'Loaded firearms are banned in or on any conveyance, but a boat that is not a motorboat is an exception. A motorboat includes anything it tows.'),
('Under the Act, which counts as a vehicle for the ban on loaded firearms?',
 'An ATV or a snowmobile', ['A canoe being paddled', 'A motorboat on open water', 'A horse being ridden'],
 'The Act defines a vehicle as anything driven, propelled or drawn on land or ice by any power, including muscle, so snowmobiles and all-terrain vehicles are vehicles.'),
('A hunter wants to use a drone to find a deer they wounded. Is that allowed?',
 'No, aircraft include drones', ['No, except to recover wounded game', 'Yes, outside hunting hours', 'Yes, if it does not herd game'],
 'Aircraft, including drones and balloons, may not be used while hunting, and the summary says that includes searching for a wounded animal.'),
('Where in Ontario is it illegal to shoot from or across a public road?',
 'Everywhere in Ontario', ['Only in the areas listed', 'Only during gun seasons', 'Only on paved roads'],
 'Discharging a firearm in or across the travelled portion of a right of way for public vehicular traffic is banned in all of Ontario.'),
('In most of southern Ontario, how close to the travelled road may a hunter carry a loaded firearm where there is no fence?',
 'No closer than 8 metres', ['No closer than 3 metres', 'No closer than 30 metres', 'Right to the shoulder'],
 'In the prescribed areas, a loaded firearm for hunting is banned on the right of way and, where there is no fence, within 8 metres of the travelled portion unless on private property.'),
('Under the Act, which is true about using a vehicle near wildlife?',
 'It may not chase or pursue it', ['It may herd game toward hunters', 'It may chase coyotes on farmland', 'It may push deer from cover'],
 'Section 24 bans using a vehicle to kill, injure, capture, harass, pursue or chase wildlife.'),
('A moose is swimming across a lake in open season. What does the Act say?',
 'It may not be hunted while swimming', ['It may be shot from a paddled canoe', 'It may be shot from the shore', 'It may be shot by a party member'],
 'Section 23 bans hunting big game, which includes moose, deer, elk, caribou and black bear, while it is swimming.'),
('A hunter rigs a rifle to fire when an animal trips a string. What does the Act say?',
 'Set firearms are banned', ['Banned only on Crown land', 'Allowed if checked daily', 'Allowed for predators only'],
 'Section 18 bans using a firearm to hunt in a manner designed to let it discharge when it is not physically held by the person.'),
('Which hunting method does the Act ban outright?',
 'Hunting with a ferret', ['Hunting with hounds', 'Hunting with a falcon', 'Hunting with a pointing dog'],
 'Section 28 bans hunting with a ferret. The Act also bans poison and adhesives to kill, injure or capture wildlife, even to protect property.'),
('Which deer lure is illegal to use or possess in Ontario?',
 'Natural deer urine', ['A synthetic deer scent', 'An acorn-based attractant', 'A doe bleat call'],
 'It is illegal to use or possess any product containing faeces, urine, blood, gland oil, saliva or other fluids of any cervid. Only synthetic or plant-based products may be used, to keep out chronic wasting disease.'),
('Which wild turkey hunting method is legal in Ontario?',
 'A hand-operated box call', ['A live hen decoy', 'An electronic gobble call', 'Hunting 300 m from bait'],
 'Section 33 bans live decoys, electronic calls and hunting within 400 metres of a place where bait has been put unless it has been free of bait for at least 7 days.'),
('A field had corn spread on it for turkeys. How long must it be free of bait before a hunter can hunt turkey within 400 metres?',
 'At least 7 days', ['At least 2 days', 'At least 30 days', 'Until the next season'],
 'A turkey may not be hunted within 400 metres of a place where bait has been deposited unless the place has been free of bait for at least seven days. Normal farming spills are not bait.'),
("How close to a dwelling may bear bait be placed without the owner's written permission?",
 'No closer than 500 metres', ['No closer than 100 metres', 'No closer than 50 metres', 'No closer than 1 kilometre'],
 'Section 56 bans placing bear bait within 500 metres of a dwelling unless the owner gives written permission, within 500 metres of a public building, or within 30 metres of a road or marked trail.'),
('How close to a public road may bait for bear hunting be placed?',
 'No closer than 30 metres', ['No closer than 5 metres', 'No closer than 500 metres', 'Anywhere off the shoulder'],
 'Bear bait may not be placed within 30 metres of a right of way for public vehicular traffic or of an established, signposted recreational trail.'),
('A bear hunter wants to hunt near a landfill. What is the rule?',
 'Not within 400 m of it', ['Not within 50 m of it', 'Allowed in the fall season only', 'Allowed on Crown land only'],
 'Section 57 bans hunting a bear within 400 metres of a waste disposal site, on Crown or private land.'),
('What may a hunter use to search for a wounded deer without a dog licence?',
 'A leashed dog, lead 10 m or less', ['A dog on a 20 m lead', 'A loose dog with a GPS collar', 'Any dog, in daylight'],
 "A dog may be used without a dog licence only to find big game already wounded in the hunt, kept on a leash no longer than 10 metres and under the handler's physical control."),
('Which big game species may never be hunted with a dog in Ontario?',
 'Elk', ['Black bear', 'White-tailed deer', 'Moose'],
 'Section 86 bans using or being accompanied by a dog when hunting elk. Dogs used to hunt deer, moose or bear must be licensed, and some areas ban them.'),
('In the parts of Ontario where the Sunday gun ban applies, what may a hunter carry on a Sunday?',
 'A long-bow or crossbow', ['A muzzle-loading shotgun', 'A shotgun for waterfowl', 'A rim-fire rifle'],
 'South of the French and Mattawa rivers, outside the listed municipalities, a person may not carry or discharge a firearm other than a long-bow or crossbow for hunting on a Sunday.'),
('North of the French and Mattawa rivers, which snare may a resident small game licence holder set?',
 'A brass wire snare for hare', ['A steel wire snare for rabbits', 'A cable snare for coyote', 'Any snare on private land'],
 'Only a resident small game licence holder may snare varying (snowshoe) hare north of the French and Mattawa rivers, with copper or brass wire of 22 to 24 gauge and a loop of 10 cm or less.'),
]
